# Link-only aliases: a name a libgcc.a member references, bound to the game
# symbol that already defines that address. One row: <libgcc name> <game symbol>.
# tools/ee/build.sh writes each row as a plain `name = symbol;` assignment into
# the link's symbol file (only when a libgcc.a is linked). It is not a
# symbol_addrs row, because activating one there makes splat rename the game
# symbol, and a matched function must keep its name (objdiff matches by name).
# A plain assignment, not PROVIDE, so landing_gate.sh's PROVIDE-stripped relink
# still resolves it. Written for task #893 (PROCEDURE #8224 §3d).
__make_fp  func_001234C0
# libm.a w_sqrt.o's imports (task #1856). Each is the ROM target of that
# relocation in the original link: __ieee754_sqrt is e_sqrt's .s (libm.a
# e_sqrt.o, still asm), matherr is libm.a s_matherr.o (game C, cod/031380),
# __errno is libc's accessor (game C, cod/015180).
__ieee754_sqrt  e_sqrt
matherr  func_00131400
__errno  func_00115200
